# BC-5 — Dedicated doc-gen Bedrock guardrail (spec 40, OQ-2)

Executor: architect (Claude). Owner approval: "validate, then proceed" 2026-07-14 —
explicit yes on the one remaining [REQUIRES-HUMAN] item (loosening PII anonymization
for the doc-gen seat only).

## Why

The agent guardrail (`cumplify-agent-guardrail-dev`) anonymizes NAME/EMAIL/PHONE.
Pointed at document generation it would redact the tenant's own company name and
quality manager out of their Quality Manual — destroying the one property (named,
specific prose) that makes the artifact credible. Spec-40 ACC-9 requires the
generated manual to carry those names unredacted AND the doc-gen guardrail to be a
distinct resource from the agent guardrail.

## What shipped

- `infra/lib/ai-stack.ts` — new `CfnGuardrail` `DocGenGuardrail`
  (`cumplify-docgen-guardrail-${env}`): PROMPT_ATTACK input HIGH retained,
  US_SOCIAL_SECURITY_NUMBER + CREDIT_DEBIT_CARD_NUMBER BLOCK retained,
  NO ANONYMIZE entries. Agent guardrail untouched.
- AI Invoker env: `DOCGEN_GUARDRAIL_ID` / `DOCGEN_GUARDRAIL_VERSION` (seat routing
  inside the invoker is spec-40 Task work — the ONE DOOR stays the one door).
- CfnOutputs: `DocGenGuardrailId` / `DocGenGuardrailVersion`.
- `infra/lib/ai-stack.unit.test.ts` — 4 new tripwires: exactly two named guardrails;
  docgen has ZERO ANONYMIZE actions but keeps SSN/card BLOCK + PROMPT_ATTACK;
  agent guardrail STILL anonymizes NAME/EMAIL/PHONE (the loosening must not leak);
  invoker env carries both seats.

